{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 58, :comments ["<b>If you do not take care to do all the words of this Torah, etc.</b> It is not satisfactory to the Master to say thus: that if you do not do all the words of the Torah, and even if you lack but a single one of them, then ״וְהִפְלָא ה׳ מַכּוֹתְךָ״ — for that is a decree the community cannot endure. And what is the meaning of what it says, ״לְיִרְאָה אֶת הַשֵּׁם הַנִּכְבָּד וְהַנּוֹרָא״ — why did it mention these epithets here more than in other places? And furthermore it is difficult: in tractate Shabbat (138a) they darshened from the verse ״וְהִפְלָא ה׳ אֶת מַכּוֹתְךָ״ that in the future the Torah is destined to be forgotten from Israel, as it says ״וְהִפְלָא ה׳״ and it is written elsewhere (Isaiah 29:14): ״לָכֵן הִנְנִי יוֹסִף לְהַפְלִיא אֶת הָעָם הַפְלֵא וָפֶלֶא וְאָבְדָה חָכְמַת חֲכָמָיו״ — but is it the way of the Holy One, blessed be He, to lock the gates of wisdom from Israel so that they perish in their iniquity?" "But surely the prophet Isaiah is speaking of a generation that fulfills the commandments — yet not from fear of HaShem, but rather on account of some external purpose that compels them to this, or on account of fear of some person who forces them to the deed against their will. And this matter causes a desecration of the Name, for without doubt the Holy One, blessed be He, searches hearts and sees that their deed is not for its own sake, and He punishes them for the evil of their thoughts. And those who see them engaged in Torah and mitzvah will cry contention against HaShem. Therefore the Sages, of blessed memory, said (Berakhot 63a): If you saw a generation for whom the Torah is not beloved, gather yourself away, etc. — they did not say 'a generation that does not study Torah at all,' but rather: they study, but not for its own sake. And therefore the Torah is not beloved unto them in essence and in the first place; rather, the imagined purpose is what is beloved to them, and one who is compelled in a matter — surely there is no love there. And in such a generation, 'gather yourself away with your pleasant words' — let no voice be heard from your mouth to teach Torah and reproof to a generation of such upheaval, whose entire Torah and deeds are nothing but from the lips outward. Also HaShem will bring about causes to destroy the wisdom of the wise from such a generation, for there is no satisfaction of spirit before Him, blessed be He, in such Torah and mitzvah." "And of this the prophet said (Isaiah 29:13–14): ״יַעַן כִּי נִגַּשׁ הָעָם הַזֶּה״ — for they are driven and coerced in all their deeds, and they do not act from fear of HaShem but rather from fear of people who compel them to the deed. And from this it follows that ״בְּפִיו וּשְׂפָתָיו כִּבְּדוּנִי וְלִבּוֹ רִחַק מִמֶּנִּי״ — for the one who compels has power to compel only regarding a matter of lips, but not regarding the intention of the heart, for who knows the hidden things of his fellow? ״וַתְּהִי יִרְאָתָם אוֹתִי מִצְוַת אֲנָשִׁים מְלֻמָּדָה״ — they call 'fear of Me' what is nothing but the command of people, for it is a command from the people who compel him to the deed and it is not the command of HaShem. ״לָכֵן הִנְנִי יוֹסִף לְהַפְלִיא אֶת הָעָם הַפְלֵא וָפֶלֶא וְאָבְדָה חָכְמַת חֲכָמָיו״ — the meaning is not that Heaven forbid the wise themselves will be lost, for it was not said ״וְאָבְדוּ הַחֲכָמִים״; nor is the meaning that the wisdom will be lost from the wise, for it was not said ״וְאָבְדָה הַחָכְמָה מֵחֲכָמָיו״; rather, the meaning is that their wisdom will be lost from the people of the generation, for HaShem will put it in their hearts not to make their voice heard abroad, and they will bring their wisdom into a generation for whom the Torah is not beloved — so that they will not know and not understand, in darkness they will walk and perish in their iniquity, since it is revealed before Him, blessed be He, that even if they were to study and act they would not study and act for its own sake. For anything done by way of compulsion has no perfection, for once the one who compels is removed, he will revert to his backsliding. Therefore HaShem commanded to make their evil known and to expose it in the congregation — regarding a generation that acts only from compulsion of some imagined purpose, such as wealth and honor, to which a man lifts his soul according to the way of our generation. Of this it says: ״אִם לֹא תִשְׁמֹר״ etc. — and He is speaking of a generation that keeps and studies and acts, but not from fear of HaShem. This is what is said: ״אִם לֹא תִשְׁמֹר לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת כָּל דִּבְרֵי הַתּוֹרָה וְגוֹ׳ לְיִרְאָה אֶת ה׳״ — meaning: you do indeed keep all the words of the Torah, but not ״לְיִרְאָה אֶת הַשֵּׁם הַנִּכְבָּד וְהַנּוֹרָא״; rather, it is from fear of the people who compel you. And you exchange and substitute the fear of the honored and awesome Name for the fear of man, grass which is given, held with cords of contempt and wrath — for you fear lest your deeds not be upright in the eyes of the people, in the way of the flatterers of our generation who act in order to find favor in their eyes, that they may honor and enrich them. Then ״וְהִפְלָא ה׳ אֶת מַכּוֹתְךָ״ — this is the wondrousness of Torah, and it will bring about that men of truth will gather the light of their Torah in a place that will not be seen and not be found, and may their lot not be among you. And then all the peoples will know that the judgments of HaShem are truth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {2 "The phrase אֱנוֹשׁ חָצִיר יִנָּתֵן הָאָחוּז בְּחַבְלֵי בּוּז וָקֶצֶף appears to weave Isaiah 51:12 (אֱנוֹשׁ כַּחָצִיר) with imagery of being bound (אָחוּז בַּחֲבָלִים); translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:14:41.211735320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}